# SOMS Backend - Supabase Connection Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env or use .NET User Secrets:
#
# Using .NET User Secrets (Recommended for local dev):
#   Run from the repository root. Replace the sample host and username with the values from Supabase Dashboard > Connect > Session pooler.
#   dotnet user-secrets set --project backend/SOMS.Api "ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection" "Host=YOUR_POOLER_HOST;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
#
# Direct Connection (Port 5432):
# ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection="Host=db.xyz.supabase.co;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
#
# Session Pooler (IPv4 compatible, port 5432; port 6543 selects transaction mode):
# ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection="Host=YOUR_POOLER_HOST;Port=5432;Database=postgres;Username=postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD;SSL Mode=Require;"
